{"article_ids": ["819549b983fd9118"], "canonical_title": "SageMaker Inference now supports Multi-Instance GPU to maximize GPU utilization for model endpoints", "category": "developer_tools", "confidence": 0.96, "description": "Amazon SageMaker Inference now supports GPU partitioning via NVIDIA Multi‑Instance GPU (MIG). The feature lets a single GPU be divided into hardware‑isolated partitions, each capable of hosting a separate model or a right‑sized fraction of the accelerator. Two optional API fields let users place one model per partition, and the post includes measurements comparing this setup to using an entire older GPU.", "entities": ["org:amazon", "org:nvidia", "term:mig", "term:nvidia"], "first_seen": "2026-11-06T18:01:00Z", "id": "evt_819549b983fd9118", "importance_score": 5.45, "last_updated": "2026-11-06T18:01:00Z", "source_ids": ["aws-machine-learning"]}
{"article_ids": ["39d0fa8ab15570a1"], "canonical_title": "How Greenlight Financial built an autonomous SOC solution on Amazon Bedrock AgentCore", "category": "ai_agents", "confidence": 0.93, "description": "Greenlight Financial created \"Luna,\" a tiered multi‑agent system built on Amazon Bedrock AgentCore that resolves more than 90% of up to 4,000 monthly security and risk cases without human intervention. The solution uses an architecture with episodic memory to enable continuous learning and is being extended from security‑operations‑center (SOC) tasks to broader financial risk triage.", "entities": ["org:amazon", "term:soc"], "first_seen": "2026-11-06T16:55:05Z", "id": "evt_39d0fa8ab15570a1", "importance_score": 5.34, "last_updated": "2026-11-06T16:55:05Z", "source_ids": ["aws-machine-learning"]}
{"article_ids": ["92b8001eea640de4"], "canonical_title": "Beyond code generation: A developer’s guide to agentic engineering", "category": "ai_agents", "confidence": 0.9, "description": "GitHub published a blog post titled “Beyond code generation: A developer’s guide to agentic engineering” that explains how developers can use GitHub Copilot not only to generate code faster but also to assist in planning work, reviewing changes, and investigating production issues, while emphasizing that human judgment remains required for many decisions.", "entities": ["product:copilot"], "first_seen": "2026-11-06T22:15:59Z", "id": "evt_92b8001eea640de4", "importance_score": 5.337, "last_updated": "2026-11-06T22:15:59Z", "source_ids": ["github-blog"]}
{"article_ids": ["0676c12db8f0f583"], "canonical_title": "How NVIDIA Open Source Tools Are Helping Researchers Build Next-Generation 6G Networks", "category": "open_source", "confidence": 0.95, "description": "NVIDIA released its Aerial wireless software as open source, joining the Sionna library and other open‑source tools aimed at accelerating next‑generation 6G network development. The combined suite gives researchers a shared foundation for testing ideas, comparing results and building on each other's work, linking simulation and AI training with real over‑the‑air wireless experiments.", "entities": ["org:nvidia", "term:nvidia"], "first_seen": "2026-11-06T16:00:35Z", "id": "evt_0676c12db8f0f583", "importance_score": 5.202, "last_updated": "2026-11-06T16:00:35Z", "source_ids": ["nvidia"]}
